# v2 = tune-1 (v1) + a LOCKDOWN role + value-aware camp choice.
# Lock role: from round 200, Tavi champions lock enemy-usable altars while the enemy leads on
# tributed gems. A lock is bought on spawn (10 gold, reserved on every champion), placed within
# 2 tiles of an altar with no visible lock, and the lock role returns home for the next one.
# Lockers attack enemy carriers nearby and guard the nearest altar once all are locked.
# Camp choice: prefer camps that give >= RICH_GEMS gems (rich_spawns), unless the camp's
# group damage (group_threat * group_hp) is too large for our health and allies. Otherwise
# take the closest camp, as in v1.
# Parent lineage: v1 (tune-1), v7zg-cast, v7-zerogem, v7, v5d-fs2, v5d, v5, v4, v3, fs-1.

# ability-type-aware casting (shield/heal on self, dash kept for escape/travel)
def cast_on(slot, u):
    if ability_ready(slot):
        if slot_is_shield(slot) or slot_is_heal(slot):
            cast_self(slot)
        elif not slot_is_dash(slot):
            cast_at_unit(slot, u)

def dash_to(slot, t):
    if ability_ready(slot):
        if slot_is_dash(slot):
            dash_towards(slot, t)

# a camp group is too dangerous when its damage over the fight exceeds our absorbable health
